      "Regulation Best Interest",
      "The SEC's Regulation Best Interest (Reg BI) goes beyond suitability. Broker-dealers and their agents must act in a retail customer's best interest and cannot put the firm's money ahead of the customer's. Accredited investors still count as retail customers. Reg BI does not apply to investment advisers, who already owe a fiduciary duty.\n\nReg BI has four obligations:\n• Disclosure: give full and fair written disclosure of material facts when recommending\n• Care: follow FINRA's suitability standards, including reasonable basis, customer-specific, and quantitative (not trading too much)\n• Conflict of interest: have procedures to address and reduce conflicts\n• Compliance: have written policies to follow Reg BI",
