      "s65-c9-paytoplay",
      "Political Contributions: Pay to Play",
      "The Pay to Play Rule stops SEC-registered advisers from donating to officials who could steer government business to them. If the adviser, a covered associate, or a PAC it controls gives such a contribution, the adviser is generally barred from paid work for that government for two years.\n\nCovered associates include partners, executive officers, and employees who seek government business, plus their supervisors. A contribution is any gift, loan, or anything of value meant to influence an election. Giving to a party or PAC is fine if it is not directed to a particular candidate.\n\nSmall gifts are allowed: up to $350 per election if the associate can vote for the official, or $150 if they cannot.\n\nAdvisers cannot pay unregulated people to seek government business for them. Only registered broker-dealers and advisers that follow similar rules may be paid. Advisers must keep records of political contributions for at least five years.",
